          "guid": "msyd3gzl6hnkjqkx",
          "message": {
            "text": "DM-2293: Preserve HarfBuzz's RETAIN_GIDS output instead of applying Domotion's private dense renumberer. Chromium and HarfBuzz treat retained glyph identity as the contract; rewriting only glyf/loca/hmtx and composite references is not a complete TrueType subset plan, and Windows demonstrated the gap as both whole-run PMingLiU Kanbun tofu and sparse Segoe UI Symbol tofu. The padded glyph-id space is an intentional correctness-over-size tradeoff; future compaction needs an upstream subset-plan mapping that rewrites every dependent structure.",
            "markdown": "DM-2293: Preserve HarfBuzz's RETAIN_GIDS output instead of applying Domotion's private dense renumberer. Chromium and HarfBuzz treat retained glyph identity as the contract; rewriting only glyf/loca/hmtx and composite references is not a complete TrueType subset plan, and Windows demonstrated the gap as both whole-run PMingLiU Kanbun tofu and sparse Segoe UI Symbol tofu. The padded glyph-id space is an intentional correctness-over-size tradeoff; future compaction needs an upstream subset-plan mapping that rewrites every dependent structure."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/embedded-font-builder.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 568,
                  "endLine": 582,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "        // second, private glyph renumbering pass; doing one here made the PUA\n        // cmap depend on our incomplete reconstruction of every TrueType table\n        // and glyph relationship. That is not equivalent even when glyf/loca\n        // and composite components look self-consistent: Windows exposed it as\n        // whole PMingLiU Kanbun runs and sparse Segoe UI Symbol composites\n        // resolving to missing-glyph boxes after an otherwise successful\n        // subset. RETAIN_GIDS is deliberately the contract, so the original\n        // gid map above is already the correct cmap target. The padded loca/hmtx\n        // space is a size cost, not a correctness defect; optimize it only with\n        // an upstream subset plan that rewrites all dependent tables.\n        let subset = hbSubsetRetainGids(bytes, gids, srcFaceIndex, true, entry.hintedSource.variationAxes ?? null);\n        // A run rendering the primary's `.notdef` box tracks GLYPH ID 0 — but a\n        // cmap entry mapping to gid 0 means \"not covered\" (the consumer browser\n        // cascades past the font and paints NOTHING, losing the tofu box).\n        // Clone the notdef outline at a fresh gid and address that instead."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ],
            "ext-ai-tool-confidence": 0.94
          },
          "workItemUris": [
            "DM-2293"
          ],
